---
import StaticPage from '@/layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
---

<StaticPage
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lead="Your data never leaves your device. Here's how MyJSONPal protects your privacy."
  metaTitle="Privacy Policy | MyJSONPal"
  metaDescription="MyJSONPal processes everything in your browser — no accounts, no data collection, no servers. Your JSON never leaves your device. Read our privacy policy."
  keywords={['privacy policy', 'json privacy', 'client side privacy', 'no data upload', 'json data protection']}
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  updated="August 1, 2026"
>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    MyJSONPal is built around a single promise: <strong>your data stays on your device</strong>.
    All tools — formatting, validation, auto-repair, minification, and every conversion — run
    entirely in your browser using JavaScript and Web Workers. There are no application servers
    that receive, process, store, or log the JSON you work with.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy explains what little information the site uses, why it is used, and the choices
    you have. If you have questions, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-never-see">What we never see</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your JSON data.</strong> Input, intermediate, and output content is processed
      locally and is never transmitted over the network.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>File contents.</strong> When you drag and drop a file, it is read directly by your
      browser and never uploaded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Account credentials.</strong> There are no accounts, no sign-ups, and no
      passwords on MyJSONPal.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="what-we-do-use">What we do use</h2>
  <p>The only data the site touches is minimal and non-identifying:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference.</strong> Your light/dark theme choice is stored in your
      browser's <code>localStorage</code> so it persists between visits. It never leaves your
      device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Page hosting logs.</strong> Like any website, the hosting provider may keep
      standard, short-lived server logs (IP address, requested URL, browser type) for security
      and reliability. These are not linked to your JSON activity.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookies-and-ads">Cookies and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    MyJSONPal does not set cookies for its own functionality. If advertising is enabled on
    the site, third-party ad networks such as Google AdSense may use cookies or similar
    technologies to serve relevant ads. These are controlled by the ad provider, not by
    MyJSONPal, and you can opt out via your browser settings or Google's Ad Settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to external resources (such as our GitHub profile). Those destinations have
    their own privacy policies and data practices, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    MyJSONPal is a developer tool and is not directed at children under 13. Because we do not
    collect personal information, there is nothing that would knowingly identify a child.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes will be reflected by an
    updated "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the site after changes
    means you accept the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your privacy? Reach out at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
